// Auto Filter (SPEC §8; Ableton Live 12's Auto Filter): a resonant filter whose cutoff an LFO and an envelope
// follower (of the input or of a sidechain) move, with five circuit models. Live publishes neither its filter
// equations nor renders we may use (SPEC §15 2026-10-24): the types and models below are documented topologies
// chosen to behave the way Live's manual describes them, adjustable later. QUESTIONS Q133 lists every choice.
//
// Signal flow (stereo, every channel alike):
//   oct  = lfoAmount·4·lfo(ch) + envAmount·8·env           octaves (lfo ±1 per channel, env = follower level)
//   fc   = clip(base·2^oct, 10 Hz, 0.49·sr)                 base = freq (DJ: from the DJ knob)
//   wet  = filter_type(x, fc, res, drive, morph)
//   out  = (x + dryWet·(wet − x)) · output
// `res` 0 … 125 %: 100 % is where the nonlinear models start to self-oscillate. Dry/wet, output and the response mix
// coefficients (which resonance and morph move) are smoothed gains (M4 review M13: 2 ms, starting at their first
// value; settled, a multiply each); the cutoff and the filters' damping step once per block, which changes the
// output's slope but not its value (the states are the analog filter's; measured in tests/stdlib/test_auto_filter.cpp).
//
// Filter types (`type`, a constant; Live 12's set as remembered):
//   0 Lowpass  1 Highpass  2 Bandpass (unity peak)  3 Notch   12 or 24 dB/oct (`slope` 0 / 1), any circuit
//   4 Morph    continuous Lowpass → Bandpass → Highpass → Notch → Lowpass over `morph` 0 … 100 %, any circuit
//   5 DJ       one knob (`dj`): left = lowpass from 20 kHz down to 25 Hz, right = highpass from 15 Hz up to 15 kHz,
//              centre = bypass (the filter fades in over the first 5 % each way); Clean, 12 / 24 dB
//   6 Comb     feedback comb y = x + fb·y[n − 1/fc], fb = 0.792·res (0 … 0.99), output · √(1 − fb²) (unity
//              power on noise); fc 20 Hz … 10 kHz is the fundamental
//   7 Resampling  sample-and-hold at 2·fc (the new Nyquist is fc), no anti-aliasing (that is the sound)
//   8 Notch + Lowpass  a notch at fc (resonance = its sharpness) into a Butterworth 12 dB lowpass at 2·fc
//   9 Vowel    three formant band-passes (Peterson–Barney vowels A E I O U, interpolated by `morph`), shifted by
//              √(fc / 1 kHz), Q 3 … 14 by res, formant gains 0 / −6 / −12 dB
//
// Circuit models (`circuit`, a constant; types 0–4; the others use Clean). Each is a zero-delay-feedback filter:
// for small signals all of them are LINEAR filters with the analytic responses below; `drive` (0 … 24 dB) sets
// how early the nonlinearity bites (the nonlinear terms see the signal × drive and their output is divided by
// drive: drive changes the character, not the level of small signals; a loud signal saturates at the input stage's
// knee, 1/drive, so OSR and SMP keep a 0 dBFS tone near −1.8 / −10 / −22 dB at drive 0 / +12 / +24 dB, PRD near 0 / −4
// / −15 dB, MS2 at 0 dB: QUESTIONS Q150).
//   Clean  TPT state-variable filter (af_svf: svf_core_fast with g per channel), k = √2·(1 − res) up to 90 % (the
//          nonlinear SVF models' law: one resonance law at the knob, M4 review M12), then exponentially down to 0.02
//          at 125 % (af_kclean): never self-oscillates (Q 0.71 … 50); drive unused (as in Live).
//   OSR    "state-variable, resonance limited by a hard-clipping diode": the SVF with k = √2·(1 − res) after a
//          soft input stage (tanh(drive·x)/drive), plus a hard diode on the band-pass state,
//          hp = x − lp − k·bp − 4·(bp − clip(bp, ±1/drive)). The equation is piecewise linear, so it is solved in
//          closed form (no Newton): the linear solution, and if |bp| passes the diode's knee, the clipped branch's.
//   MS2    "Sallen-Key, soft clipping limits the resonance" (MS-20-like): the SVF whose positive resonance
//          feedback saturates, hp = x − lp − 2·bp + (2 − k)·tanh(drive·bp)/drive; `solve`, 2 Newton iterations
//          from the linear solution (within −120 dB of the converged solution at +12 / +24 dB drive; 1 iteration
//          would be −46 … −66 dB).
//   SMP    a custom design between MS2 and PRD: PRD's saturating input stage and MS2's saturating resonance
//          feedback, made asymmetric (even harmonics), hp = tanh(drive·x)/drive − lp − 2·bp +
//          (2 − k)·a(drive·bp)/drive, a(v) = tanh v + tanh² v / 4; `solve`, 2 iterations (as MS2).
//   PRD    a four-pole transistor ladder (Moog/Prodigy-like) with the saturating input pair and no other resonance
//          limiting: u = tanh(drive·(x − 4·res·y4))/drive into four TPT one-poles. The feedback divides the low
//          passband by 1 + 4·res (−6.8 dB at the default 30 %); the output adds 4·res·(wLP + wN)·y4, which restores
//          unity there for the lowpass and notch (M4 review M12: the models' levels match within 1 dB at the default
//          resonance, tested). `solve` on y4, 1 Newton iteration from the linear solution (measured within −120 dB of
//          the converged solution even at +24 dB drive).
//          Responses: Oberheim-Xpander pole mixing of (u, y1 … y4): LP4 y4, LP2 y2 (12 dB = the 2-pole tap of the
//          same ladder), HP (1−G)ⁿ, BP 4G²(1−G)² / 2G(1−G), notch (1 − 2G + 2G²)^(n/2).
// The SVF models' outputs mix (x, bp, lp): lp, hp = x − k·bp − lp, bp·kb (kb = k for Clean, max(k, 0.25) for the
// nonlinear models, so their self-oscillation stays audible), notch = x − k·bp. 24 dB = a fixed Butterworth SVF
// section (k = 1.848, Clean) into the model's section with k·0.5412 (Butterworth-4 at res 0).
// Self-oscillation (res 125 %; renders at 22.05 / 48 / 192 kHz, drive 0 and +24 dB: finite and bounded, peak ≤ +8
// dBFS; at +24 dB drive the oscillation is ~1/drive as loud): at a 1 kHz cutoff PRD oscillates within 0.5 c of it,
// MS2 3–11 c flat, SMP 24–40 c, OSR 33–76 c (12 / 24 dB; their nonlinearity sits in the band-pass state: an
// amplitude-dependent detuning, as in the analog circuits; up to ~2 semitones near Nyquist at 22.05 kHz). The comb (type 6) is in tune: its impulse response repeats every sr/fc samples (spectral
// peaks within 0.01 c up to 2.5 kHz, −4 c at 7 kHz from the delay line's linear interpolation).
//
// LFO (`lfo: 1` turns it on; a constant: off costs nothing): `lfoShape` 0 sine, 1 triangle, 2 saw up, 3 saw down,
// 4 square, 5 random (sample-and-hold, a new value each cycle and at the start); the shapes with jumps (saws,
// square, random) go through a 0.5 ms one-pole, so a jump of the cutoff does not click (measured: the filter's
// largest step then equals the analog filter's on the same cutoff path). Rate free (0.01 … 40 Hz) or synced to the
// song (`lfoSync`, one cycle per `lfoBeats` beats); `lfoOffset` shifts both channels' phase, `lfoPhase` the right
// channel's against the left, `lfoSpin` speeds the right channel up by 0 … 50 %. Envelope follower (`env: 1`):
// peak follower (stdlib envfollow) of the mono input, attack / release time constants; with `scOn: 1` it
// listens to the `sc` input (gain `scGain`, mixed with the own input by `scMix`). `sc` is the device's sidechain
// input: unconnected it is silence; T4.7 routes a track into it.
//
// Exports: `cutoff` (the modulated cutoff, Hz, per channel), `lfoSignal` (the LFO, ±1 per channel), `envelope`.
//
// Cost: the cutoff is param rate (coefficients once per block) unless the LFO or the follower is on; then the
// coefficient math (one fast_exp, one fast_tan, a divide per section) runs per sample. Clean: one SVF core per
// section; OSR: the same plus a compare and two divides; MS2 / SMP / PRD: a 1-unknown Newton solve per sample
// (bench/RESULTS.md T4.11: Clean ≈ 6–11, OSR ≈ 17–21, PRD ≈ 70–75, MS2 / SMP ≈ 100–110 ns per stereo sample).
import "../dynamics/envfollow.pqp"
import "../control/smooth.pqp"
import "../filters/circuit.pqp"     // the circuit models af_osr, af_ms2, af_smp, af_ladder (shared with Operator)

patch auto_filter {
  in    x         : audio stereo
  in    sc        : audio stereo = (0, 0)   // sidechain input (silence until routed, T4.7)
  in    type      : real const = 0          // 0 LP 1 HP 2 BP 3 Notch 4 Morph 5 DJ 6 Comb 7 Resampling 8 Notch+LP 9 Vowel
  in    circuit   : real const = 0          // 0 Clean 1 OSR 2 MS2 3 SMP 4 PRD
  in    slope     : real const = 0          // 0: 12 dB/oct, 1: 24 dB/oct
  in    lfo       : real const = 0          // 1: LFO on
  in    lfoShape  : real const = 0          // 0 sine 1 triangle 2 saw up 3 saw down 4 square 5 random
  in    env       : real const = 0          // 1: envelope follower on
  in    scOn      : real const = 0          // 1: the follower listens to the sidechain input
  param freq      = 1kHz  [20Hz..20kHz]   @unit(Hz) @curve(exp) @label("Frequency")
  param res       = 30%   [0%..125%]      @label("Resonance")
  param drive     = 0dB   [0dB..24dB]     @unit(dB) @label("Drive")
  param morph     = 0%    [0%..100%]      @label("Morph")
  param dj        = 0%    [-100%..100%]   @label("DJ")
  param lfoAmount = 0%    [0%..100%]      @label("Amount")
  param lfoRate   = 1Hz   [0.01Hz..40Hz]  @unit(Hz) @curve(exp) @label("Rate")
  param lfoSync   = false                 @label("Sync")
  param lfoBeats  = 1     [1/16..64]      @curve(exp) @label("Beats")
  param lfoOffset = 0%    [0%..100%]      @label("Offset")
  param lfoPhase  = 0%    [0%..100%]      @label("Phase")
  param lfoSpin   = 0%    [0%..50%]       @label("Spin")
  param envAmount = 0%    [-100%..100%]   @label("Amount")
  param attack    = 6ms   [0.1ms..100ms]  @unit(s) @curve(exp) @label("Attack")
  param release   = 200ms [1ms..3s]       @unit(s) @curve(exp) @label("Release")
  param scGain    = 0dB   [-24dB..24dB]   @unit(dB) @label("SC Gain")
  param scMix     = 100%  [0%..100%]      @label("SC Mix")
  param dryWet    = 100%  [0%..100%]      @label("Dry/Wet")
  param output    = 0dB   [-24dB..24dB]   @unit(dB) @label("Output")
  out   out : audio stereo

  // ---- modulation (octaves) ----
  det  = scOn >= 0.5 ? x + scMix * (sc * scGain - x) : x
  e    = envfollow(0.5 * (det[0] + det[1]), attack, release)
  lr   = af_lfo(lfoShape, lfoRate, lfoSync, lfoBeats, lfoOffset, lfoPhase, lfoSpin)
  l    = lfoShape >= 1.5 ? smooth(lr, 0.5ms) : lr        // the shapes with jumps: de-clicked (0.5 ms one-pole)
  oct  = (lfo >= 0.5 ? lfoAmount * 4 * l : 0) + (env >= 0.5 ? envAmount * 8 * e : 0)

  // DJ: the knob's cutoff (left: lowpass 20 kHz → 25 Hz, right: highpass 15 Hz → 15 kHz).
  djc  = dj < 0 ? 20000 * fast_exp(6.684611727667927 * dj) : 15 * fast_exp(6.907755278982137 * dj)
  base = type > 4.5 && type < 5.5 ? djc : freq
  fc   = lfo + env >= 0.5 ? clip(base * fast_exp(0.6931471805599453 * oct), 10, 0.49 * sr) : clip(base, 10, 0.49 * sr)
  g    = fast_tan(3.141592653589793 * fc / sr)

  // ---- response weights of the SVF / ladder types: LP, BP, HP, notch ----
  p    = 4 * morph
  hLP  = max(0, 1 - abs(p)) + max(0, p - 3)
  hBP  = max(0, 1 - abs(p - 1))
  hHP  = max(0, 1 - abs(p - 2))
  hN   = max(0, 1 - abs(p - 3))
  djHP = dj > 0 ? 1 : 0
  wLP  = mux(type, 1, 0, 0, 0, hLP, 1 - djHP)
  wBP  = mux(type, 0, 0, 1, 0, hBP, 0)
  wHP  = mux(type, 0, 1, 0, 0, hHP, djHP)
  wN   = mux(type, 0, 0, 0, 1, hN, 0)
  d    = circuit >= 0.5 ? drive : 1

  // ---- the types ----
  model = type > 4.5 ? 0 : circuit
  filt  = af_filter(x, model, slope, g, res, d, wLP, wBP, wHP, wN)
  djw   = min(1, 20 * abs(dj))
  djOut = x + djw * (filt - x)
  comb  = af_comb(x, fc, res)
  rsmp  = samplehold(x, af_wrap(min(2 * fc, 0.45 * sr)))
  nlp   = af_notch_lp(x, fc, g, res)
  vowel = af_vowel(x, fc, res, morph)
  w     = mux(type, filt, filt, filt, filt, filt, djOut, comb, rsmp, nlp, vowel)

  out = gain(gain_add(x, w - x, dryWet, start: 1), output, start: 1)

  export cutoff    = fc
  export lfoSignal = l
  export envelope  = e
}

// The LFO: two phases (left, right), one shape. Free: phasors at rate and rate·(1 + spin); synced: the song
// position, one cycle per `beats` beats (the right channel `1 + spin` times faster). `offset` shifts both phases,
// `phase` the right one.
patch af_lfo {
  in    shape  : real const = 0
  param rate   = 1Hz  [0.01Hz..40Hz] @unit(Hz)
  param sync   = false
  param beats  = 1    [1/16..64]
  param offset = 0    [0..1]
  param phase  = 0    [0..1]
  param spin   = 0    [0..0.5]
  out   y : audio stereo

  fl  = phasor(rate)
  fr  = phasor(rate * (1 + spin))
  sl  = frac(transport.beat / beats)
  sr_ = frac(transport.beat * (1 + spin) / beats)
  pl  = frac((sync ? sl : fl) + offset)
  pr  = frac((sync ? sr_ : fr) + offset + phase)
  y   = (af_shape(pl, shape), af_shape(pr, shape))
}

// One LFO shape at phase p (0..1), bipolar; every shape starts like the sine (0 or its cycle start at p = 0).
patch af_shape {
  in    p     : audio
  in    shape : real const = 0
  out   y : audio

  sine   = sine(p)
  tri    = 4 * abs(frac(p + 0.75) - 0.5) - 1
  sawUp  = 2 * frac(p + 0.5) - 1
  sawDn  = 1 - 2 * frac(p + 0.5)
  square = p < 0.5 ? 1 : -1
  rnd    = samplehold(noise(), p < z1(p) || z1(1) < 0.5)   // a new value at each cycle start (and at the first sample)
  y = mux(shape, sine, tri, sawUp, sawDn, square, rnd)
}

// True for the one sample per cycle where a phasor at `hz` wraps (hz < sr/2).
patch af_wrap {
  in    hz : audio
  out   y : bool

  ph = phasor(hz)
  y  = ph < z1(ph)
}

// Types 0–5: the circuit model at 12 dB (one section) or 24 dB (a Butterworth pre-section, then the model).
// `model` 0 Clean, 1 OSR, 2 MS2, 3 SMP, 4 PRD; w* the response weights.
patch af_filter {
  in    x     : audio
  in    model : real const = 0
  in    slope : real const = 0
  in    g     : audio
  param res = 0.3    [0..1.25]
  param d   = 1      [1..16]
  param wLP = 1      [0..1]
  param wBP = 0      [0..1]
  param wHP = 0      [0..1]
  param wN  = 0      [0..1]
  out   y : audio

  clean = model < 0.5
  k12 = clean ? af_kclean(res) : 1.4142135623730951 * (1 - res)
  kB  = slope >= 0.5 ? 0.541196100146197 * k12 : k12
  kbB = clean ? kB : max(kB, 0.25)
  a   = af_sec(x, 0, g, 1.8477590650225735, 1.8477590650225735, 1, wLP, wBP, wHP, wN)
  b   = af_sec(slope >= 0.5 ? a : x, min(model, 3), g, kB, kbB, d, wLP, wBP, wHP, wN)
  lad = af_ladder(x, slope, g, 4 * res, d, wLP, wBP, wHP, wN)
  y   = model > 3.5 ? lad : b
}

// One SVF section of model 0–3 and its output mix: y = (wHP + wN)·x + (kb·wBP − k·(wHP + wN))·bp + (wLP − wHP)·lp.
patch af_sec {
  in    x     : audio
  in    model : real const = 0
  in    g  : audio
  param k  = 1.4142 [-1..100]
  param kb = 1.4142 [0..100]
  param d  = 1      [1..16]
  param wLP = 1 [0..1]
  param wBP = 0 [0..1]
  param wHP = 0 [0..1]
  param wN  = 0 [0..1]
  out   y : audio

  c  = af_svf(x, g, k)
  o  = af_osr(x, g, k, d)
  m  = af_ms2(x, g, k, d)
  s  = af_smp(x, g, k, d)
  bp = mux(model, c.band, o.band, m.band, s.band)
  lp = mux(model, c.low, o.low, m.low, s.low)
  hn = wHP + wN
  y  = gain_add(gain_add(gain(x, hn, start: 1), bp, kb * wBP - k * hn, start: 1), lp, wLP - wHP, start: 1)
}

// Clean's damping (M4 review M12: one resonance law): k = √2·(1 − res), the nonlinear models' law, up to 90 %
// (Q 0.71 … 7.1); above, where those self-oscillate, Clean's k falls exponentially to 0.02 at 125 % (Q 50) and stays
// a stable linear filter.
patch af_kclean {
  param res = 0.3 [0..1.25]
  out   k : audio

  k = res < 0.9 ? 1.4142135623730951 * (1 - res) : 0.1414213562373095 * fast_exp(-5.545177444479562 * (res - 0.9))
}

// Comb: y = x + fb·y[n − T], T = 1/fc (fc 20 Hz … 10 kHz), fb = 0.792·res; the output scaled by √(1 − fb²).
patch af_comb {
  in    x  : audio
  in    fc : audio
  param res = 0.3  [0..1.25]
  out   y : audio

  fb  = 0.792 * res
  yc  = x + fb * delay(yc, 1 / clip(fc, 20, 10000), 50ms)
  y   = yc * sqrt(1 - fb * fb)
}

// Notch + Lowpass: an SVF notch at fc (k = Clean's resonance law) into a Butterworth SVF lowpass at 2·fc.
patch af_notch_lp {
  in    x  : audio
  in    fc : audio
  in    g  : audio
  param res = 0.3    [0..1.25]
  out   y : audio

  k  = af_kclean(res)
  n  = af_svf(x, g, k)
  nt = x - k * n.band
  g2 = fast_tan(3.141592653589793 * min(2 * fc, 0.49 * sr) / sr)
  y  = af_svf(nt, g2, 1.4142135623730951).low
}

// Vowel: three formant band-passes (unity peak) at the vowel's formants × √(fc / 1 kHz), gains 1, 1/2, 1/4.
// `morph` 0 … 1 goes A → E → I → O → U (linear in Hz between neighbours). Q = 3 + 9·res.
patch af_vowel {
  in    x  : audio
  in    fc : audio
  param res   = 0.3  [0..1.25]
  param morph = 0    [0..1]
  out   y : audio

  q  = 4 * morph
  i  = min(floor(q), 3)
  f  = q - i
  f1 = mux(i, 730, 530, 270, 570) + f * (mux(i, 530, 270, 570, 300) - mux(i, 730, 530, 270, 570))
  f2 = mux(i, 1090, 1840, 2290, 840) + f * (mux(i, 1840, 2290, 840, 870) - mux(i, 1090, 1840, 2290, 840))
  f3 = mux(i, 2440, 2480, 3010, 2410) + f * (mux(i, 2480, 3010, 2410, 2240) - mux(i, 2440, 2480, 3010, 2410))
  sh = sqrt(fc * 0.001)
  k  = 1 / (3 + 9 * res)
  b1 = af_svf(x, af_warp(f1 * sh), k).band
  b2 = af_svf(x, af_warp(f2 * sh), k).band
  b3 = af_svf(x, af_warp(f3 * sh), k).band
  y  = k * (b1 + 0.5 * b2 + 0.25 * b3)
}

// The prewarped integrator gain of a frequency kept in [20 Hz, 0.45·sr].
patch af_warp {
  in    f : audio
  out   g : audio

  g = fast_tan(3.141592653589793 * clip(f, 20, 0.45 * sr) / sr)
}

// stdlib svf_core_fast (filters/svf_fast.pqp) with the integrator gain g as an input, so it may differ per channel
// (the LFO's stereo phase): the same TPT SVF, the state update two multiply-adds deep.
patch af_svf {
  in    x : audio
  in    g : audio
  param k = 1.4142 [-1..100]
  out   band : audio
  out   low  : audio

  a1 = 1 / (1 + g * (g + k))
  d1 = -2 * g * (g + k) * a1
  b1 = 2 * g * a1
  b2 = b1 * g

  v   = x - ic2
  n1  = b1 * v + (d1 * ic1 + ic1)
  n2  = b2 * v + (b1 * ic1 + ic2)
  ic1 = z1(n1)
  ic2 = z1(n2)

  band = 0.5 * (ic1 + n1)
  low  = 0.5 * (ic2 + n2)
}
